      <memberdef kind="enum" id="_marmot_material_hughes_winget_8h_1aae3da5caf189b7df4924e17c1ac99260" prot="public" static="no" strong="yes">
        <type></type>
        <name>HughesWingetTangent</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::Materials::HughesWingetTangent</qualifiedname>
        <enumvalue id="_marmot_material_hughes_winget_8h_1aae3da5caf189b7df4924e17c1ac99260a8503d71dcafbdc254c2bbea2599e5791" prot="public">
          <name>Analytic</name>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Closed-form linearisation of the Hughes-Winget update, assuming <formula id="7">$ \partial\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{(n+1)}/\partial\boldsymbol{\sigma}_{\text{rot}} = \boldsymbol{I} $</formula>. Exact while the wrapped material responds elastically. One wrapped-material evaluation. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="_marmot_material_hughes_winget_8h_1aae3da5caf189b7df4924e17c1ac99260a1649aed298f99d587e2eb30c1db5946b" prot="public">
          <name>Exact</name>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>As HughesWingetTangent::Analytic, but the operator <formula id="8">$ \boldsymbol{S} = \partial\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{(n+1)}/\partial\boldsymbol{\sigma}_{\text{rot}} $</formula> is recovered by forward-differencing the wrapped material with respect to its six incoming stress components. Fully consistent. Seven wrapped-material evaluations. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="_marmot_material_hughes_winget_8h_1aae3da5caf189b7df4924e17c1ac99260a5225763efc97aebd39e5a303fceb57ac" prot="public">
          <name>Numerical</name>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>The complete update is forward-differenced with respect to the nine components of <formula id="9">$ \boldsymbol{F} $</formula>. Fully consistent and model-agnostic, but the most expensive option (eleven wrapped-material evaluations). Intended for verification and debugging. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Selects how the algorithmic tangent <formula id="0">$ \partial\boldsymbol{\tau}/\partial\boldsymbol{F} $</formula> of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_hughes_winget_wrapper" kindref="compound">Marmot::Materials::HughesWingetWrapper</ref> is evaluated. </para>
        </briefdescription>
